<title>SPAIN: Spain Social Security fund won't hit deficit - Rato.</title>
<headline>Spain Social Security fund won't hit deficit - Rato.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said on Wednesday that short-term funding of 168 billion pesetas to compensate for a short-fall at Social Security will not affect this year's deficit, according to a local news agency.</p>
<p>Rato, speaking at a trade fair, said the funding should be approved at Friday's cabinet meeting, news agency EFE reported.</p>
<p>The government has forecast an overall deficit to gross domestic product this year of 4.4 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
